Grafana is an open-source monitoring and data visualization platform used to analyze system performance and display metrics through interactive dashboards.
It connects to various data sources, such as Prometheus, InfluxDB, and MySQL, to retrieve and visualize data.

The main features of Grafana are:
- Dashboards: Display monitoring information in a single interface.
- Panels: Present data using graphs, charts, tables, and gauges.
- Data Sources: Provide access to metrics and other data.
- Alerts: Notify users when specified conditions are met.
- Variables: Allow users to dynamically filter and explore dashboard data.
Grafana helps monitor application performance, identify system failures, and support effective decision-making through real-time visualization.

